// The connection of the Jet SQLite engine and the objects it owns: a port
// of the SQLite 3.45.0 sqliteInt.h and vdbeInt.h structures (struct sqlite3,
// Db, Schema, Table, Column, Index, FKey, Trigger, FuncDef, CollSeq,
// Savepoint, VTable, Vdbe, VdbeOp, VdbeCursor, VdbeFrame, SubProgram,
// AuxData, sqlite3_context), hash.c, and the schema lookups and unlinks of
// callback.c and build.c the virtual machine needs.
//
// C's pointers are arena indexes here, -1 for NULL: a Table is an index of
// Conn.tables, an Index of Conn.indexes, a Trigger of Conn.triggers, an FKey
// of Conn.fkeys, a Schema of Conn.schemas, a VTable of Conn.vtables, a Btree
// of Conn.btrees and a prepared statement of Conn.vdbes. Freed slots go on
// the arena's free list and are reused. The expressions, lists and selects
// the schema objects hold live in the connection's AST arena (ast.AST).
//
// Ephemeral btrees (OP_OpenEphemeral) are Conn.btrees slots too, so that
// every cursor names its btree by one index; the database files are the
// btrees that Db.bt names. Each Btree keeps a copy of the connection state
// it reads (btree.BtDB); sync_btrees refreshes them where C would have read
// the changed sqlite3 fields through its pointer.
//
// A collating sequence is its record.COLL_* id; CollSeq names the builtins
// (BINARY, NOCASE, RTRIM) and any registered later get the next ids.

use {
    base: __core_db_base
    util: __core_db_util
    btree: __core_db_btree
    record: __core_db_record
    ast: __core_db_ast
    rowset: __core_db_rowset
    sorter: __core_db_sorter
}

